{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1006","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Two Strings Swaps"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two strings $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ consisting of lowercase English letters, both of length $$$n$$$. The characters of both strings have indices from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, inclusive. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are allowed to do the following "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose any index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$) and swap characters $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose any index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$) and swap characters $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_{n - i + 1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose any index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$) and swap characters $$$b_i$$$ and $$$b_{n - i + 1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that if $$$n$$$ is odd, you are formally allowed to swap $$$a_{\\lceil\\frac{n}{2}\\rceil}$$$ with $$$a_{\\lceil\\frac{n}{2}\\rceil}$$$ (and the same with the string $$$b$$$) but this move is useless. Also you can swap two equal characters but this operation is useless as well."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to make these strings equal by applying any number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" described above, in any order. But it is obvious that it may be impossible to make two strings equal by these swaps."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess move"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can replace a character in $$$a$$$ with another character. In other words, in a single "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess move"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" you can choose any index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), any character $$$c$$$ and set $$$a_i := c$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find the minimum number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to apply in such a way that after them you can make strings $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ equal by applying some number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" described in the list above."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" you make after the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" does not matter. Also note that you cannot apply "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the string $$$b$$$ or make any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" after the first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"change"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is made."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the length of strings $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains the string $$$a$$$ consisting of exactly $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains the string $$$b$$$ consisting of exactly $$$n$$$ lowercase English letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the minimum number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"preprocess moves"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to apply before "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", so that it is possible to make the string $$$a$$$ equal to string $$$b$$$ with a sequence of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"changes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the list above."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\nabacaba\nbacabaa\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text"